INSTRUCTION 367: Extract one object per signoff person. Create separate objects for each signer.

DEFINITION: A "signoff person" executes, adopts, or authorizes the document. Includes:
- Signatures with printed name and title below
- "IN WITNESS WHEREOF" signature blocks
- Executive signatories (CEO, CFO, Chairman, etc.)

EXCLUDE: Individuals merely listed in body, exhibits, or schedules unless also signing the main document.

FIELDS TO EXTRACT:

1. NAME: Full legal name of signer (below signature line or signature block)
2. DESIGNATION: Title/role (below name, or inferred from document context). Use "NA" if unclear.

OUTPUT JSON STRUCTURE:

{
  "Signoff_Persons": [
    {
      "Name": "Ola Källenius",
      "Designation": "Chairman of the Board of Management"
    },
    {
      "Name": "Harald Wilhelm",
      "Designation": "Chief Financial Officer"
    }
  ]
}
